{"text": "Ogunbanjo & Trask, PC - Audit A-2026-044180 - PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL TAXPAYER INFORMATION\n\nOgunbanjo & Trask, PC\nCertified Public Accountants\n735 Broad Street, Suite 900, Chattanooga, TN 37402 | 423-555-0140 | www.ogunbanjotrask.example\nJune 18, 2026\nVIA TNTAP UPLOAD AND FIRST-CLASS MAIL\nDarnell Fitzsimmons, Tax Auditor II\nTennessee Department of Revenue, Field Audit Division\n1301 Riverfront Parkway, Suite 203, Chattanooga, TN 37402-2740\nRe: Saltgrass Kitchen Supply, LLC - Sales and Use Tax Account No. 104-882-617 - FEIN 62-1849073 - Audit No. A-2026-044180 - Audit period 07/01/2022 through 06/30/2025\nDear Mr. Fitzsimmons:\nWe represent Saltgrass under the Power of Attorney filed February 9, 2026. This letter responds to the Notice of Proposed Assessment dated May 20, 2026, letter ID L0448217733, which proposes additional tax of $84,316.22, interest of $13,907.51 and a negligence penalty of $8,431.62, for a total of $106,655.35. The Taxpayer disagrees with three of the four schedules and asks for an informal conference under Tenn. Code Ann. § 67-1-1438 before the 30-day period ends on June 19.\n1. Schedule A - Exempt sales disallowed ($41,720.00 tax)\nThe sample disallowed 36 invoices for lack of a certificate. We now enclose (Exhibit A) completed Streamlined Sales and Use Tax Certificates of Exemption for the buyers below. Each was a registered dealer buying for resale or an exempt school at the time of sale.\nCustomer\tInvoices\tCertificate / account no.\tSales\nMoccasin Bend Barbecue Co.\tSK-20418, SK-20977, SK-23104\t103-447-290\t$118,400.00\nSeong Restaurant Holdings LLC\tSK-21556 and 11 others\t105-019-833\t$203,912.40\nSignal Mountain Country Day School\tSK-22871\texemption EX-0077418\t$27,645.00\nChickamauga Lake Marina & Grill\tSK-24402, SK-24403\tnone obtained\t$9,880.00\n\nThe Taxpayer concedes the last line (tax $913.90). Hyun-woo Seong, managing member of the Seong group, has signed an affidavit that every item was installed in his restaurants for use in preparing food for sale; Mr. Seong can be reached at 423.555.0176.\n2. Schedule B - Unreported sales from deposit analysis ($29,188.72 tax)\nThe auditor compared deposits to the operating account at Lookout Valley Bank & Trust (account ending *6610) with sales on Form SLS 450 and treated the $315,553.73 difference as taxable. Exhibit B reconciles it:\n$180,000.00 on 03/14/2023: proceeds of the SBA-backed loan, no. LV-7720418-02, not sales.\n$96,250 in four transfers from the member's personal account (ending 2204): capital contributions by Lorenzo Battaglia after his divorce settlement was funded in August 2023. The transfers appear on the Form 1065 capital account.\n$31,400.00 on 11/02/2024: insurance recovery for the Rossville Boulevard warehouse flood, claim CP-24-1180337.\n$7,903.73: Shopify payouts already included in reported sales (timing).\nAfter these items no unreported sales remain.\n3. Schedule C - Use tax on out-of-state purchases ($11,502.50 tax)\nAgreed except for the forklift bought in Dalton, Georgia, on 9/6/24 for $38,900 (serial F18D-04417K). Georgia tax of $2,723 was paid at purchase and credit is due under Tenn. Code Ann. § 67-6-409.\n4. Penalty\nThe negligence penalty should be waived. The Taxpayer has filed and paid every period on time since registering in 2019. The errors arose in the spring of 2023, when Mr. Battaglia was hospitalized for six weeks after a stroke and the books were kept by his daughter, Caterina Battaglia, then a college sophomore. Caterina did not know certificates had to be kept on file.\nRequested result\nRevised tax of $9,693.40 plus interest, no penalty. A check for that amount (no. 10482) can be issued on agreement. Please direct questions to me at wogunbanjo@ogunbanjotrask.example or my direct line, (423) 555-0141. Mr. Battaglia prefers not to be called at the store; his cell is 423-555-0109 and his home address for any notice is 88 Fairy Trail, Lookout Mountain, TN 37350.\nRespectfully,\nWinnifred Ogunbanjo, CPA (TN license no. 38417)\ncc: L. Battaglia, Managing Member", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "615 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Darnell Fitzsimmons", "Hyun-woo Seong", "Lorenzo Battaglia", "Caterina Battaglia", "Winnifred Ogunbanjo"], "companies": ["Ogunbanjo & Trask", "Saltgrass Kitchen Supply, LLC", "Tennessee Department of Revenue", "Moccasin Bend Barbecue Co.", "Seong Restaurant Holdings LLC", "Signal Mountain Country Day School", "Chickamauga Lake Marina & Grill", "TNTAP", "Seong group", "Lookout Valley Bank & Trust", "Shopify", "Tenn."]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 1.5, "modelMs": 36049.60000000149, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "Ogunbanjo & Trask, PC", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Ogunbanjo & Trask, PC"}, {"start": 30, "end": 43, "text": "A-2026-044180", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "A-2026-044180"}, {"start": 96, "end": 117, "text": "Ogunbanjo & Trask, PC", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Ogunbanjo & Trask, PC"}, {"start": 128, "end": 146, "text": "Public Accountants", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Public Accountants"}, {"start": 147, "end": 174, "text": "735 Broad Street, Suite 900", "kind": "street", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "735 Broad Street, Suite 900"}, {"start": 176, "end": 191, "text": "Chattanooga, TN", "kind": "places", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Chattanooga, TN"}, {"start": 192, "end": 197, "text": "37402", "kind": "zip", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "37402"}, {"start": 200, "end": 212, "text": "423-555-0140", "kind": "phone", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "423-555-0140"}, {"start":